Long sword and katana to expert - 5  Snick or Excal 'nuff said
Two weapon wield to expert - 6 Whack them more often samurai style
Bow to expert - 5 Just like a samurai in a movie thin their ranks from
a distance
Silver saber to basic - 1 As soon as one comes available drop the
original katana

That's 17 and to me that might be the minimum set for an
ascendable samurai.  But there are other ones to varying
degree of importance -

Dagger to basic - 1 I think i've done this in every samurai
game so far as it is very beneficial in the early game.  A
stack of daggers does not disappear so use them until the
arrows are blessed and your luck maxed.

Broad sword usually elven broadsword to skilled - 3 I think
I've enhanced to basic but not skilled in several games.
There are plenty of elven broad swords in the game but
few silver sabers so this makes an okay secondary wield
until a silver saber comes available.  Elven broad swords
are inherently rustproof like silver saber unlike long sword
or katana (but not fireproof) so they work well when not
fixed with either rustproof Snickersnee or Excalibur as the
primary wield.

Attack spells to basic - 1  Getting cold as a beam sure
helps on wet levels but it's definitely optional.

Polearm to skilled - 3 Getting into the options that are
strictly fun.  Use a spetum at Ft Ludious and you can earn
enough points to be offered all the way up to skilled to be
ready at the Castle.  Definitely fun rather than critical.

Martial arts to GM - All the points you'll have left and then
some.  Chuckle.  Not harmful to spend points for fun, but
not critical either.  Fixed kicking boots aren't as good as
jumping or speed boots so this one ends up very far down
the importance scale, but if you're not going to wield the
ToM two handed so you never enhance two handed sword
you might end up with spare slots to burn ...


